    # used by both 'shap' and 'shapiq') and the three new 'shapiq'-only
    # fields (19, 20, 21) - with 'Marker effect method' (16) LAST in that
    # group, immediately before 'Return marker effect for interactions?'
    # (5). This exactly mirrors RKHS/SVR/KNN's own established pattern
    # above: every method-specific/shared sub-field for a section sits
    # BEFORE that section's own method selector, and the method selector
    # itself sits immediately before the NEXT section's toggle (RKHS's
    # 'Marker effect method' (17) is likewise placed after its own
    # iml_shapley-only fields (6, 7) and before its internal fan-out
    # fields (8, 9); SVR's 'Marker effect method' (22) sits after its own
